:{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116620","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116620","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116620.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116620.patch","merged_at":"2026-03-23T21:45:25Z"},"body":"This PR:\r\n- adds local billboarding (X or Y axis)\r\n- fixes billboarding ignoring custom axis\r\n- adds rotation velocity3d\r\n\r\nSupersedes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116363 and https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113838\r\n\r\nWhile working on the axis rotation, I had some doubts about the implementation. In particular, we are given feedback over and over regarding how confusing the placement of our properties is. I felt like rotation around axis being placed with the billboards was going to be very counter intuitive for people. Initially, I just wanted to verify that adding 3d rotation velocity on top of axis rotation would still work with the velocity alignmnet done in the copy shader. And, well, it didn't.\r\n\r\nBetween the unintuitive property placing and the fact that adding 3d rotation velocity later would not have been compatible with the work I did, i decided to remove angle over life in transform align for 3d and just add 3d rotation velocity. I'm not happy that I couldn't give something better than what other particle systems offer, but if anything this explains why it's done that way. \r\n\r\nIt's gone a long distance from the initial proposal ( https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/13747 ) but this is what needs to be implemented for the feature to be the easiest to use it can.","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_ur